    <completed>2026-07-22</completed>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>
    Build the client half of the R4 bridge (design §5, "Capture (frontend)"): intercept ProseMirror
    transaction steps and map EACH step to an operation anchored `(paraId, runIndex, run-local-offset)`
    per the task-003 operation schema. This is a NEW ProseMirror plugin/extension under
    `src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/` — it does NOT diff the document and does NOT emit
    `{paraId,text}` payloads. Borrow the `prosemirror-transform` primitives (`Step`, `StepMap`, `Mapping`)
    per `notes/bridge-prior-art.md` §1; reuse the existing `widgets/paraIdExtension.ts` to read a node's
    `w14:paraId` attribute — do NOT re-mint ids here. Resolve, for a given editor position, the enclosing
    paraId node, the index of the run it falls in, and the run-local offset (the fine anchor D2 mandates).
    An edit expressed against an opaque atom node (task 021's non-editable node) MUST be refused, not
    captured. Explicitly: MIT ProseMirror base APIs only — NO `@tiptap-pro/*`, no AGPL (NFR-03). All this
    task adds is capture; it neither fetches nor saves (that is the save-path tasks' job).
  </prompt>

  <role>
    Senior React/TypeScript editor engineer fluent in ProseMirror internals (transactions, `Step`/`StepMap`,
    `ResolvedPos`, node/mark schema) and the TipTap extension model. Understands invariant I-6 (the client is
    a view + controller that EMITS operations, never authors bytes) and D2 (anchor by
    `(paraId, runIndex, run-local-offset)`, never absolute editor positions).
  </role>

  <goal>
    A ProseMirror plugin/extension that, on every editor transaction, produces zero or more operations —
    each a valid task-003 op anchored `(paraId, runIndex, run-local-offset)`. A typed edit at an interior
    location inside a paragraph emits an operation whose anchor resolves back to exactly that
    `(paraId, runIndex, offset)`; the legacy `{paraId,text}` payload shape is never produced; an edit that
    ProseMirror routes into an opaque atom is refused (atoms are non-editable). Rebasing across a continuing
    session is task 022's job — this task produces correctly-anchored per-transaction operations.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      Design §5.0 (the bridge is the real work; its hard pieces are opaque atoms, offset→run mapping, and
      structural ops) and §5 "Capture (frontend)" (intercept transaction steps → operations
      `{paraId, offset|range}`; DELETE the `getHTML`/paragraph-diff export). The op schema this maps onto is
      task 003 (FR-11) — the shared spine both ends compile against. The durable coarse anchor is the node's
      `w14:paraId` (already carried by `widgets/paraIdExtension.ts`); the fine anchor is
      `(runIndex, run-local-offset)` because a bare char-offset drifts when an earlier same-paragraph edit
      lands first (the CRDT/Peritext lesson, `notes/bridge-prior-art.md` §4). This task REPLACES the retired
      `collectEditedParagraphs` paragraph-diff capture (`utils/docxBridge.ts:330-395`) — but does NOT delete
      it here (that is task 023, gated on the Phase 0 gate 006). Capture only; no save wiring.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="new">src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/widgets/stepOperationInterceptor.ts — NEW ProseMirror plugin/TipTap extension: transaction steps → task-003 operations anchored `(paraId, runIndex, run-local-offset)`</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/widgets/paraIdExtension.ts — reuse to read the enclosing node's `w14:paraId` attr; do NOT re-mint ids here</file>
      <file role="dependency-output">projects/spaarkeai-compose-r4/tasks/003-operation-schema.poml output — the versioned operation contract (op types + `{paraId, runIndex, offset|range}` anchor) this maps onto</file>
      <file role="modify">src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/widgets/ComposeEditor.tsx — register the interceptor extension in the editor schema/plugin list (wire-in only; no save-path change here)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/utils/docxBridge.ts:330-395 — the retired `collectEditedParagraphs` this supersedes (read for the behaviors to cover; do NOT delete — task 023)</file>
      <file role="design">projects/spaarkeai-compose-r4/design.md §5, §5.0 (the bridge; offset→run mapping)</file>
      <file role="design">projects/spaarkeai-compose-r4/notes/bridge-prior-art.md §1 (ProseMirror Step/StepMap/Mapping), §4 (anchor drift)</file>
      <file role="spec">projects/spaarkeai-compose-r4/spec.md FR-03, FR-11, NFR-02, NFR-03</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="003" status="pending">Operation schema (FR-11) — the shared op types + `{paraId, runIndex, offset|range}` anchor this interceptor emits. MUST exist before mapping.</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="spec / FR-03">Editor edits MUST be captured as operations anchored `(paraId, runIndex, run-local-offset)` from ProseMirror transaction steps. MUST NOT emit any `{paraId,text}` payload and MUST NOT re-diff paragraph text. Scope: the capture plugin only.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project / I-3, I-6, I-7">Anchor by `w14:paraId` + run-index + run-local-offset ONLY; never a text-search, never an absolute editor position as the durable anchor. The client is a view+controller that emits operations; it authors no bytes. Scope: this interceptor and its emitted ops.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project / D2">The fine anchor MUST be `(runIndex, run-local-offset)`, re-derivable on apply — NOT a bare `(paraId, char-offset)` — to survive an earlier same-paragraph edit. Scope: the anchor resolver in this module.</constraint>
    <constraint source="spec / FR-02">An edit expressed against an opaque atom node (task 021) MUST be refused, not captured (atoms are non-editable and never opened). Scope: the interceptor's per-step guard.</constraint>
    <constraint source="spec / NFR-03">MIT ProseMirror base + `@tiptap/extension-*` only. MUST NOT add `@tiptap-pro/*`, AGPL, or any commercial/per-seat package, and MUST NOT take a runtime dependency on EigenPal. Scope: this task's imports/package.json.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-028">Any client fetch introduced uses `@spaarke/auth` (`useAuth`/`authenticatedFetch`). NOTE: this task adds NO fetch — capture only; flagged so no ad-hoc token handling is introduced.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038 / NFR-06">Capture behavior is covered by Vitest unit tests colocated in the shared lib (authored fully in task 024); this task's own tests exercise the anchor-resolution + atom-refusal behavior. NO `Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;`, DI-registration, or ctor-null tests. Scope: tests colocated under `src/`.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>ProseMirror transaction/step interception; offset→run anchor resolution; TipTap extension registration; paraId identity; client licensing discipline</topic>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-028-spaarke-auth-architecture.md</file>
      <file>docs/adr/ADR-038-testing-strategy.md</file>
