      <file>projects/spaarkeai-compose-r4/design.md</file>
      <file>src/client/shared/CLAUDE.md</file>
    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="paraId node attr read" location="src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/widgets/paraIdExtension.ts">
        The extension that carries `w14:paraId` as a hidden node attr on `paragraph`/`heading` (PARAID_NODE_TYPES). Read the enclosing node's paraId from a ResolvedPos via this attr — reuse, do not re-mint.
      </pattern>
      <pattern name="Step/StepMap/Mapping" location="notes/bridge-prior-art.md §1">
        `prosemirror-transform` provides invertible atomic `Step`s and `Mapping.map(pos,bias)` — iterate a transaction's steps and resolve each changed range to `(paraId, runIndex, offset)`. In-session only; durable identity is the paraId.
      </pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <justification>
    <existing>The retired `collectEditedParagraphs` (`utils/docxBridge.ts:330-395`) is the only current capture path and it is paragraph-diff, `{paraId,text}`-coarse — verified by grep against `Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/`. No existing module intercepts ProseMirror steps or resolves run-local offsets.</existing>
    <extension>`collectEditedParagraphs` cannot be extended into step-level capture without discarding its entire paragraph-diff algorithm — it re-diffs whole paragraph text and has no notion of runs, offsets, or structural ops. Replacing (not extending) it is the correct move; extending would keep a second text-coarse path alive (the exact defect R4 removes).</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Without step-level capture there are no structural edits and every delta re-diffs runs, so the FR-03 acceptance "interior typed edit → operation with correct `(paraId,runIndex,offset)`" is unachievable and the Patch Engine has no ID-anchored operations to apply — the drift class returns.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Output the FULL rigor-level declaration (root §8). Load the knowledge files + `notes/bridge-prior-art.md` + the task-003 operation-schema output. Confirm task 003 is complete (the op contract exists to map onto). Note this is a capture-only client task (no fetch, no save wiring, no deletion).</step>
    <step order="1" name="Anchor resolver">Implement, in `stepOperationInterceptor.ts`, a resolver: given a ProseMirror position/ResolvedPos, return `(paraId, runIndex, run-local-offset)` — paraId from the enclosing PARAID_NODE_TYPES node via `paraIdExtension`, runIndex + run-local-offset by walking the node's inline runs (mark-boundary runs) accumulating length until the offset lands. Re-derivable, per D2.</step>
    <step order="2" name="Step→operation mapping">Iterate each transaction's `Step`s; map each to a task-003 operation (insertText / deleteRange / replaceRange / setMark/clearMark / structural where the step expresses one), anchored via the step-1 resolver. Emit no `{paraId,text}` payloads.</step>
    <step order="3" name="Opaque-atom guard">Add the guard: a step whose target resolves into an opaque atom node (task 021) is refused (no operation emitted; the atom stays non-editable). Checkpoint (context-handoff) after this third step per root §5.</step>
    <step order="4" name="Register in editor">Register the interceptor extension in `ComposeEditor.tsx`'s plugin/extension list (wire-in only). Do NOT touch the save path or delete the legacy export (task 023).</step>
    <step order="5" name="Local tests + build">Add colocated Vitest tests for the anchor-resolution + atom-refusal behaviors (task 024 authors the full suite). Run `npm run build:prod` (NOT `npm run build`) for the shared lib; confirm green and no `@tiptap-pro/*` in the dependency tree.</step>
    <step order="6" name="Close-out">Update `tasks/TASK-INDEX.md`: set this task's status to ✅. Document any deviation in `projects/spaarkeai-compose-r4/notes/`.</step>
  </steps>

  <ui-tests>
    <ui-test name="Interior typed edit emits correct anchor">
      <steps>Mount ComposeEditor on a projected doc; place the caret mid-word inside a formatted paragraph (a run boundary present) and type a character.</steps>
      <expected>One operation is emitted whose anchor resolves to the enclosing paragraph's `paraId`, the correct `runIndex`, and the exact run-local `offset`; no `{paraId,text}` payload appears.</expected>
    </ui-test>
    <ui-test name="Edit inside an opaque atom is refused">
      <steps>With a doc containing an opaque atom node (field/SDT placeholder), attempt to type inside the atom.</steps>
      <expected>No operation is emitted and the atom content is unchanged (non-editable); the caret cannot author into the atom.</expected>
    </ui-test>
    <ui-test name="Multi-run paragraph offset maps to the right run">
      <steps>In a paragraph split into bold + normal runs, type at the boundary between them.</steps>
      <expected>The emitted operation's `runIndex`/`run-local-offset` identifies the correct run and in-run position (not an absolute doc position).</expected>
    </ui-test>
    <ui-test name="Dark-mode render (ADR-021)">
      <steps>Render ComposeEditor with the interceptor registered under the Fluent v9 dark theme provider and perform an edit.</steps>
      <expected>The editor surface and any atom placeholders use theme tokens and are legible in dark mode; capture behavior is identical to light mode; no hard-coded light colors.</expected>
    </ui-test>
  </ui-tests>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If ProseMirror expresses an edit (a `Step`) that the task-003 operation schema cannot represent — e.g. a step shape with no corresponding op type — STOP and surface it (root §6 / §6.5) as a schema gap; do NOT silently drop the step or invent an out-of-contract op.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/widgets/stepOperationInterceptor.ts (new ProseMirror step→operation interceptor)</output>
    <output type="code">src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/widgets/ComposeEditor.tsx (interceptor registered)</output>
    <output type="test">Colocated Vitest tests for anchor resolution + atom refusal (extended in task 024)</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria testable="true">
    <criterion testable="true">An interior typed edit emits an operation whose anchor resolves to the correct `(paraId, runIndex, run-local-offset)`.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">No `{paraId,text}` payload and no paragraph-diff capture is produced by the new interceptor.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">An edit routed into an opaque atom node is refused — no operation emitted, atom unchanged (negative case).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">In a multi-run paragraph, the emitted `runIndex`/`run-local-offset` identifies the correct run and in-run position (not an absolute editor position).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">No `@tiptap-pro/*` / AGPL / EigenPal runtime dependency is introduced; `npm run build:prod` for the shared lib is green (NFR-03).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The dark-mode render (ADR-021) is legible with theme tokens; capture behavior is theme-independent.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>
    Capture only — no fetch (so no `@spaarke/auth` call here), no save wiring, no deletion. The legacy
    `collectEditedParagraphs` is removed in task 023 (gated on the Phase 0 gate 006), not here. Rebasing the
    op log across a continuing session is task 022. Client task (no BFF surface) — no publish-size / CVE gate.

    COMPLETION (2026-07-22):
    - New: `src/widgets/stepOperationInterceptor.ts` — read-only ProseMirror plugin (headless TipTap extension
      `StepOperationInterceptor` + `createStepInterceptorPlugin` factory). Exports `resolveRunAnchor`,
      `runsOfBlock`, `runLocalPoint`, `classifyStep`. Uses MIT `@tiptap/pm/{state,model,transform}` only (no
      new package, no `@tiptap-pro/*`). Anchors ops `(paraId, runIndex, run-local-offset)` per D2; never
      emits `{paraId,text}`.
    - New: `src/widgets/stepOperationInterceptor.test.ts` — 18 colocated jest tests (all green): interior-edit
      anchor, multi-run boundary, mark mapping, deleteRange/replaceRange, setBlockAttr(Alignment),
      atom-refusal (schema-driven guard), unrepresentable-mark escalation, live plugin capture, no-mutation.
    - Wired additively into `ComposeEditor.tsx` (`...COMPOSE_R4_STEP_INTERCEPTOR`, bare/no-handler — wire-in
      only) and barrel `src/index.ts`. Did NOT touch task 021's opaque-atom node file or its schema line.
    - Quality gates: code-review + adr-check PASS (0 critical, 0 violations).

    DEVIATIONS (directional-mode, per root §8.5 / POML `<steps mode="directional">`):
    1. Test runner is JEST (`npm test`), not Vitest — the package harness is jest (`jest.config.js`,
       `compose-operations.test.ts` precedent). Ran via jest; ADR-038 colocation + banned-test rules honored.
    2. Build verified via `npm run typecheck` (`tsc --noEmit`) rather than `npm run build:prod` — this shared
       lib has NO `build:prod` script (`build` = `tsc`); parent instruction confirmed `npm run build`.
       typecheck used to avoid a `dist/` write-lock collision with the concurrent task-021 build. My files
       type-clean; remaining `tsc` errors are pre-existing (unbuilt `@spaarke/*` sibling `dist/` in this
       worktree — environmental, not introduced by task 020).
    3. Structural ops (split/merge/insertParagraph/deleteParagraph, list wrap, non-alignment block attrs) are
       recognized and routed to the `onStructuralStep` seam for task 031 (structural-operations) — never
       silently dropped, never mis-mapped. This is the correct 020/031 boundary.
    4. ADR-021 dark-mode ui-test: the interceptor is a headless capture plugin (no DOM, no color) →
       theme-independent by construction; asserted at the capture layer. The visible dark-mode chrome check
       belongs to task 021's atom placeholder NodeView.
  </notes>

